### `streamlit_callbacks.py`

`StreamlitStepHandler` — a LangChain callback handler that writes short status lines (e.g. "🔧
Using **search**...", "💭 Thinking...") into a Streamlit `st.status` box as the agent works, so
you see live progress instead of a blank spinner during a normal (non-deep-research) run.
Requires the Streamlit script-run context to be explicitly attached to the background thread the
agent runs in (`add_script_run_ctx` in `research_agent.py`) — without that, these callbacks fail
silently with a `NoSessionContext` error, since Streamlit widgets don't know which page/session
they belong to when called from an arbitrary thread.

