## Environment Variables

| Variable | Required? | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `GOOGLE_API_KEY` | **Yes** | Gemini API key from [aistudio.google.com/apikey](https://aistudio.google.com/apikey). Must start with `AIza` — a Cloud Console OAuth client ID/secret will *not* work here. |
| `GROQ_API_KEY` | No | Enables automatic fallback if Gemini's quota/rate limit is hit. Free key at [console.groq.com](https://console.groq.com). |
| `GROQ_FALLBACK_MODELS` | No | Comma-separated override of which Groq models to try, in order. Default: `llama-3.3-70b-versatile,llama-3.1-8b-instant,openai/gpt-oss-120b`. |
| `TAVILY_API_KEY` | No | Licensed search backend. Without it, falls back to DuckDuckGo scraping (fine for personal use, not licensed for commercial use). Free key at [tavily.com](https://tavily.com). |
| `SUPABASE_URL` / `SUPABASE_KEY` | No | Enables Supabase-backed history storage instead of local SQLite. Both must be set together. |
| `APP_PASSWORD` | No | If set, gates the entire app behind a password prompt — useful before deploying publicly. |

`GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS`, if present in your shell environment from unrelated Google
Cloud SDK setup, is automatically ignored by this app (see `build_agent_executor()` in
`research_agent.py`) since it otherwise breaks Gemini authentication.

